\section*{Structured Abstract}

\textbf{Background:}
Tissue regeneration requires coordinated stability across cellular proliferation, scaffold
mechanics, and metabolic-immune balance.

\textbf{Methods:}
We developed the Sovereign Regenerative Engine (SRE), enforcing four invariants:
proliferation control, scaffold stability, metabolic balance, and immune suppression.

\textbf{Results:}
Under 50,000-cycle adversarial stress testing, all invariants remained satisfied. No neoplastic
drift, no scaffold failure, and full metabolic recovery were observed.

\textbf{Conclusion:}
The SRE provides a mathematically stable conceptual framework for tissue reconstruction.

